    definition: "The goal of a legible AI interface is not to make the user trust it more. It's to make their trust match how trustworthy the system actually is, action by action. When perceived trustworthiness tracks real reliability, reliance tracks reliability too. Both over-trust (relying on it when it's wrong) and under-trust (ignoring it when it's right) are failures the design caused.",
