    technical: "Bucinca and Gajos showed that passive explanations raise reliance without improving decision accuracy, because users treat the existence of a rationale as a quality signal and stop scrutinizing. The mechanism is that reading an explanation is low-effort and confirmatory: it gives the brain a reason to accept what it already wanted to accept. The design consequence is that an explanation panel which the user can passively consume is not a legibility feature, it's a deference amplifier. Legibility requires the explanation to expose a checkable fact or force an action (a cognitive forcing function), not just to be present and readable.",
